{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggK65tf5aVjW2QSmHMmj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the full 100 grosze is accounted for.\n\nThe cause was that `split_cents` used floor division only (`total // people`) and never distributed the remainder. The fix in `money.py` uses `divmod` and gives one extra grosz to the first `remainder` people:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1] * remainder + [share] * (people - remainder)\n```\n\nIn `test_money.py` I added two tests first and confirmed they failed:\n- `test_remainder_is_distributed`: `split_cents(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`\n- `test_shares_sum_to_total`: for totals 0–499 and 1–11 people, the shares sum to the total\n\nAll 5 tests in `test_money` pass now.\n\nChoice I made: the extra grosze go to the first people in the list, so the larger shares come first. If you'd rather the rounding favour someone else, such as the payer, that's a one-line change. I did not commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":779,"cache_read_input_tokens":22163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":779},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da9867ad-7188-414a-a2a0-03325b236f46","uuid":"d553cade-a724-41be-bcac-85f8d4296ed0","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:30:17.610Z","request_id":"req_011CggK65eHKwxbDwWUdCHPD"}
